-- title:
--   Original true stopped Gaussian pre/post gradient right-dividend first-Hermite expected atom energy has explicit root-physical-mesh bound
-- statement:
--   For the original topcap zero-jump Gaussian Lévy stochastic dividend process, arbitrary strictly pre-ruin bounded stop rho, positive source C² reserve band and actual physical m grid, the true expected nonnegative right-payment pre/post Gaussian gradient error is bounded uniformly by K sqrt(n/(m+1)). This is the concrete stochastic source-rate estimate obtained from the original discounted right-atom telescoping budget, Proved true stopped-history Gaussian weighted second moments and first-moment Young inequality and compact actual gradient Lipschitz; it is stronger than the parent L1 limit and retains genuine X,D,ruin and stop.
-- source:
